course: dictionary
lesson: 11673
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word «assignment» is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «Our history assignment is due on Monday.» The words due on Monday tell you an assignment is a piece of school work, given to do at home or over several days. Try the meaning in the sentence: "Our history piece of work is due on Monday." That still makes sense.
explain: «Ben's assignment at the newspaper was to interview the mayor.» Here an assignment is a job given at work. The words at the newspaper and to interview the mayor are your clues.
fact: An assignment is a piece of work a teacher gives you to do, often at home or over several days.
fact: «Assignment» can also mean a job or task someone is given at work.
fact: In a formal way, assignment can mean giving something to someone or putting it in a place, as in «the assignment of seats».
fact: The verb «assign» means to give someone a job or to decide where something should go.
fact: When you are not sure which meaning is right, look at the rest of the sentence and check the clues.
exercise: «Our history assignment is due on Monday.» What is an assignment in this sentence? | A holiday trip | A loud noise | *A piece of school work to hand in | A type of football kit
exercise: «Ben's assignment at the newspaper was to interview the mayor.» What does assignment mean here? | A kind of cake | *A job or task given at work | A long rest | A secret game
exercise: The teacher read out «the assignment of seats» for the trip. What does assignment mean in this phrase? | *Giving each person a place | Mixing up the chairs | Stealing a seat | Sitting down quickly
test: «The class got a new assignment about rainforests, due next Friday.» What does assignment mean? | A rainy-day game | *A piece of work given to do at home | A quiet corner | A birthday present
test: «The spy received a secret assignment to find the map.» What does assignment mean here? | A boring lesson | A map of the town | A thick jacket | *A task given to someone
exam: Read this: «Please hand in your assignment by Friday.» Which meaning is right? | A type of pen | A party invitation | A lost bag | *Work a teacher gives you to finish
